# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jaesun Kim et al. (2026). Optimizing cross-domain transfer for universal machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-026-70195-8  arXiv:2510.11241v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2510.11241v3 (sha256 1b3f756877a27376...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 76 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the universal multi-task model 7net-Omni (SevenNet-MF
# architecture) trained by curriculum learning on sixteen databases from
# inorganic crystals, catalysts, MOFs and molecules (242 million
# structures; Table 1), and its intermediate model 7net-ompa trained on
# MPtrj, sAlex and OMat24. Benchmark results are spread over many tasks
# and figures and are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

